Article 2 (Use of Police Body-Worn Recording Devices) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 10-5 (1) 9 of the Act on the Performance of Duties by Police Officers (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means any of the following cases:
1. Where verbal abuse, assault, etc. has occurred or is likely to occur in the course of a police officer's performance of duties under Article 2 of the Act (limited to police public officials; the same shall apply hereinafter);
2. Where it is urgently necessary to prevent or restrain any of the following acts:
(a) Abuse of an older person under Article 1-2, subparagraph 4, of the Welfare of Senior Citizens Act;
(b) Child abuse under Article 3, subparagraph 7, of the Child Welfare Act;
(c) Violence against women under Article 3, subparagraph 1, of the Framework Act on Prevention of Violence against Women;
(d) Abuse of a person with disabilities under Article 2 (3) of the Act on Welfare of Persons with Disabilities;
(e) Reoffending by a prisoner or parolee who is the subject of information notified under Article 126-2 of the Administration and Treatment of Correctional Institution Inmates Act or Article 55-3 of the Act on Probation;
(f) A retaliatory crime against a crime reporter, etc. under Article 2, subparagraph 3, of the Act on Protection of Specific Crime Informants;
3. Where it is urgently necessary to collect evidence for a criminal investigation or to document a scene at any of the following places; provided, in cases under items (a) and (c), this shall be limited to cases where urgent collection of evidence for a criminal investigation is necessary:
(a) A site where traffic law violations are being enforced under the Road Traffic Act;
(b) A site where a police officer issues an order to release illegally caught fishery resources under Article 16 of the Fishery Resources Management Act;
(c) A site of an assembly or demonstration under the Assembly and Demonstration Act;
(d) A site where compliance with Article 3 of the Act on the Regulation of Amusement Businesses Affecting Public Morals is inspected under Article 9 of that Act;
(e) A site where measures to protect maritime navigation are taken under Article 14 (1) of the Maritime Security Act;
4. Where the following activities are conducted and a crime, if committed, is expected to have a significant social impact:
(a) Protection of important persons under Article 2, subparagraph 3, of the Act;
(b) Counterterrorism activities under Article 2, subparagraph 6, of the Act on Anti-Terrorism for the Protection of Citizens and Public Security;
5. Where it is urgently necessary to take measures or issue orders to ensure smooth traffic flow and prevent traffic hazards at the site of a disaster under Article 3, subparagraph 1, of the Framework Act on the Management of Disasters and Safety;
6. Other cases deemed clearly and urgently necessary to protect a person's life, bodily integrity, or property.
